<h2 id="measurables">Height, Weight &amp; Wingspan</h2>
<p>Kelce measured 6-foot-4 7/8 and 255 pounds at the pre-draft process ahead of the 2013 NFL Draft, with a wingspan of 6-foot-8 — a 3.5-inch difference between his height and his reach, a genuine length advantage at the position. His arm length came in at 33.75 inches with a 9.625-inch hand span, both well above average for a tight end and part of what makes him such a difficult target to strip the ball from or jam at the line.</p>
