<h2 id="jumps">Vertical and Broad Jump: The Explosiveness Numbers</h2>
<p>Kelce's 35-inch vertical jump and 10-foot-4 broad jump are arguably more revealing than his straight-line speed. Both numbers point to real lower-body power — the kind that shows up as the ability to high-point a contested catch over a defender, or to explode off the line and gain immediate separation before a linebacker can get his hands on him. Combined with his size and length, it's a profile built for exactly the kind of matchup nightmare Kelce became over his career.</p>
