<h2 id="context">The Bigger Picture</h2>
<p>Kelce went in the third round, 63rd overall, in 2013 — not because the numbers weren't there, but because a shortened pre-draft process due to injury left some uncertainty for teams. Andy Reid and the Chiefs took the swing anyway, and the athletic tools that showed up at his pro day — size, length, speed, and explosiveness all in one package — turned into one of the most productive tight end careers in NFL history.</p>
