<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Why didn't Travis Kelce run at the NFL Combine?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Kelce underwent sports hernia surgery in January 2013, ahead of the combine, which prevented him from working out in Indianapolis. His athletic testing numbers instead came from his Cincinnati pro day roughly six weeks later.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Is a 4.61-second 40 fast for a tight end?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Yes. At nearly 255 pounds, a 4.61 is well above average for the tight end position, where the historical average sits closer to 4.70 seconds. It placed Kelce among the faster testers at the position in his draft class.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">How tall is Travis Kelce?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Kelce measured 6-foot-4 7/8 at the pre-draft process, with a 6-foot-8 wingspan — a notably long reach relative to his height.</div>
